{"page": "8", "label": "[5]", "page_scribes": ["Joseph Smith Jr.", "Oliver Cowdery", "Unidentified"], "segments": [{"scribe": "Oliver Cowdery", "js_hand": false, "text": " ✦"}, {"scribe": "Oliver Cowdery", "js_hand": false, "text": "["}, {"scribe": "Joseph Smith Jr.", "js_hand": true, "text": "5.28"}, {"scribe": "Oliver Cowdery", "js_hand": false, "text": "]In the first degree Ah-broam—signifies The father of the faithful, the first right, the elders second degree—same sound—A follower of rightiousness— Third degree—same sound—One who possesses great Knowledge— Fourth degree—same sound—A follower of righteousness, a possessor of greater Knowledge. Fifth degree—Ah-bra-oam. The father of many nations, a prince of peace, one who keeps the commandments of God, a patriarch, a rightful heir, a high priest. W\nW [] [p. [5]]\n"}]}
